AB  - The aim of this study was to determine the physiological profile of young triathletes who began triathlon competition as their first sport, Twenty-nine male competitive triathletes (23 regionally and nationally ranked triathletes and 6 elite, internationally ranked triathletes) performed two tests, one on a cycle ergometer (CE (V)over dotO(2max)) and one on a treadmill (TM (V)over dot(2max)). Results showed (a) no difference between CE (V)over dot(2max) and TM (V)over dotO(2max) in the triathletes (69.1 +/- 7.2 vs. 70.2 +/- 6.2 mL . kg(-1) . min(-1), respectively), (b) values of CE (V)over dot(2max) and TM (V)over dotO(2max), in elite triathletes (75.9 +/- 5.2 and 78.5 +/- 3.6 mL . kg(-1) min(-1), respectively) that were comparable to those reported in elite single-sport athletes in these specialities, and (c) although the ventilatory threshold (Th-vent) was similar in CE and TM, Th-vent was consistently lower for triathletes than TM Th-vent usually reported for runners.
